    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0404" n="373" xml:id="pg373"/>

                <head>107. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Poindexter) to President Reagan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d107-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1986-05-23">May 23, 1986</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Draft NSDD on Interim Restraint</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">Issue</p>
                <p>Should you approve the draft NSDD on U.S. interim restraint policy at <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tab A</hi>?<anchor n="2" xml:id="d107-f2"/></p>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">Background</p>
                <p>The draft NSDD is based upon the draft Presidential statement which we discussed
                    on Wednesday.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d107-f3"/></p>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">Discussion</p>
                <p>The NSDD differs from the Presidential statement only in that it adds some
                    additional detail to some of the taskings and addresses the issue of encryption
                    which should be kept out of the public record.</p>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">Recommendation</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">OK NO</hi></p>
                <p>___ ___ That you approve and sign the draft NSDD at <hi rendition="#italic">Tab
                        A</hi>.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d107-f4"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d107-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d107-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Security Council, National Security Council Institutional Files,
                    Box SR–093, NSDD–227. Secret. Sent for action. Prepared by Linhard and Kraemer.
                    Reagan wrote his initials in the upper right-hand corner of the memorandum. A
                    stamped notation at the top of the memorandum reads: “Signed.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d107-f2" n="2" xml:id="d107-f2-content">
                <p>Printed as <ref target="#d108">Document 108</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d107-f3" n="3" xml:id="d107-f3-content">
                <p>May 21. Reagan met with Shultz and Poindexter in the Oval Office from 1:28 until
                    1:56 p.m. (Reagan Library, President’s Daily Diary) No minutes were found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d107-f4" n="4" xml:id="d107-f4-content">
                <p>Reagan initialed his approval and wrote a checkmark next to his initials.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
